September the 19th will see the first  funeral for a British monarch in decades  here is what you need to know  State funeral is held for people of  national significance usually monarchs  they include pageantry haunt and  ceremony usually with religious and  Military aspects  the last person to have a state funeral  was Winston Churchill in 1965. other  notable people include the Queen's  father King George VI Admiral Nelson and  Sir Isaac Newton  Prince Philip the Queen Mother and Diana  Princess of Wales had large televised  ceremonies but despite having a lot of  similarities they were not State  funerals  I don't think our City's ever seen  the sort of presence we're going to see  over the next few days this is a  military operation like any other we  plan it we rehearse it and then we  execute it and that I think helps with  the pressure the funeral will take place  on Monday the 19th of September here at  Westminster Abbey heads of state Prime  Ministers and presidents European Royals  and key figures from public life will  all be invited to gather in the Abbey  which can hold 2 000 people a bank  holiday has been declared on the day of  the funeral so schools will be closed  and many businesses and shops but a day  off isn't a right on a bank holiday  that's down to individual employers  after the funeral the Queen's coffin  will be taken to Saint George's Chapel  at Windsor Castle for a committal  service the queen will then be buried  alongside Prince Philip in the King  George VI Memorial Chapel  if you haven't got an invitation to the  funeral you can still watch some of it  on the morning of the funeral the  Queen's coffin will be taken from the  Palace of Westminster where it's lying  in state to Westminster Abbey in a  ceremonial procession Chief mourners now  move out to follow Diana Princess of  Wales members of the royal family are  going to walk behind the coffin like  they did for Prince Philip and Princess  Diana  the public can go and watch that part  but big Crowds Are expected so expect  some very long cues and of course if you  want you can still watch it all on  television
 

